     "text": "Worker shutdown in acme-platform: on SIGTERM the worker stops taking jobs and drains in-flight ones with a 30s grace period (GRACE_PERIOD_MS in services/worker/src/shutdown.ts), matched by terminationGracePeriodSeconds: 30 in infra/helm/worker/values.yaml. Pods get killed mid-job during deploys: image-resize jobs can exceed 30s and w.close() can still pick up one more job. Priya says it is on our side; proposed fix (not yet made): pause workers before close and raise both values together (e.g. 90s app, 100s Helm).",
     "kind": "fact",
     "entities": [
      "worker",
